## World Extensions

Extensions are runtime-only capabilities attached to a `World`.

Use them to attach event listeners, adapters, runtimes, diagnostics, virtuals, or other world-local behavior that should be installed once.

```js
import { World, defineExtension } from "./index.js";

const debugLogging = defineExtension("debugLogging", world => {
  const offDamage = world.on("damage", payload => {
    console.log("damage", payload);
  });

  return () => {
    offDamage();
  };
});

const world = new World();

